      "narrative": "Mara's eyebrows twitch \u2014 the smallest tell that you've asked something pointed. She turns her head, not quite looking at Toran Vex but gesturing toward him with her chin.\n\n\"You're looking at him.\" She says it flat, like it should have been obvious. \"Toran Vex. Lockwright of the Kestrel Guild. He kept that lock oiled and true for the better part of a decade.\" Her voice drops a little. \"He's also the one who sealed it on the Kestrel's orders. Same hands that maintained it, same hands that locked it.\"\n\nAcross the room, at a scarred table near the shuttered window, Toran Vex flinches at the mention of his name. His quill scratches a jagged line across his ledger. He doesn't look up.\n\nMara watches you process that, then adds, quieter now: \"He hasn't talked about it since. Not to me, not to anyone.\" She lets that hang. \"You want to know what happened at that Gate, he's the one who turned the key. Whether he'll turn his tongue is another question.\"\n\nShe tilts her cup toward you. \"Your move.\""
    },
