      "narrative": "Your voice cuts through the damp air \u2014 \"Old Bram!\" \u2014 and bounces off the stone wall, flattening against the iron seal, then bleeding out into the mist beyond.\n\nThe sound dies quickly. No echo returns from the other side. No answering call. The mist swallows your voice like a stone dropped into deep water.\n\nThe *Grey Hind* rocks gently against the dock. The iron seal holds its silence. A single drop of water falls from the stone arch above you and lands on the black disc with a soft *tick*.\n\nNothing stirs. No footsteps approach. No voice calls back.\n\nThe Ash Gate remains sealed, the mist remains thick, and the ferryman who worked this crossing for twenty-three years is not here to answer. He hasn't been for a long time."
